      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Ambiguous heading: read as salted neats' (ox) tongues from the provisions context of the Quebec export lists and CUST 4 ('Meats viz Tongues'); cod tongues are entered separately as 'Tongues and Sounds'.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_meats_provisions; wd_term=NONE): Tongues exported from Quebec in kegs / by number and in lbs sit in the provisions list beside beef and pork (cf. htc:1378 'Meats viz Tongues' in the same CUST 4 ledgers); fish tongues are separately headed 'Tongues and Sounds' (htc:0513). Layer-1 observations: 257 rows, 1807–1897. Series: KEW_CUST 4 ×45; CSP_Canadian Trade and Navigation ×16; CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×196. Units: Kegs ×126; Lbs. (Pounds) ×68; Number ×30; (no unit) ×18. Top routes: Canada → England ×27; Quebec QC → Great Britain ×26; Quebec → All Countries ×23; Quebec → Great Britain ×19.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
        {
