      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an emburet of iron commonly known as black lead, and also called graphite, used for making crucibles and leads for pencils; we import large quantities from Ceylon. A genus of plants with acrid, caustic properties. *See* **LEAD-WORK**. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 305]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
