      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "wicks covered with solidified oil or fat, for giving light. There are many varieties, dips and moulds being chiefly tallow, while hard and composition candles are made of spermaceti, stearine, paraffine, wax, or palm oil. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 77]",
