      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the commercial name for the bony matter of the tusks of the elephant, the teeth of the hippopotamus and walrus, the horn of the narwhal, &c. Elephant Ivory is the most esteemed, and that obtained in the largest quantity; our imports are nearly 500 tons a-year. Ivory is largely [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 218]",
