      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_alcoholic_beverages; processing_state=refined_extract; land_basis=terrestrial_forest): Essence of spruce is the concentrated decoction used to make spruce beer (Simmonds 1892 s.v. SPRUCE: foliage 'used ... to give flavour to beer, either in the form of decoction or extract'); exported from Quebec in boxes/kegs/gallons. Not timber. Layer-1 observations: 121 rows, 1807–1871. Series: KEW_CUST 4 ×96; HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×2; CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×23. Units: (no unit) ×82; Gallons ×18; Boxes ×9; Kegs ×4. Top routes: Canada → England ×35; Canada → Scotland ×19; Canada → Great Britain ×19; Quebec QC → Great Britain ×18.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "oe:firstAttested/#resource": 1807,
