      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_64_66_89_Paper_Glass_Misc_Manufactures",
      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Gemälde, Schilder-eyen. Du. Schilderyen. DA. Malerie, Skilderie. Sw. Mälningar. FR. Tableaux. IT. Pitture, Quadri. SP. Pinturas, Cuadros. PORT. Pinturas. RUS. Kartinü. POL. Nalowania.*) The taste for foreign paintings and pictures having lately surprisingly decreased, our inland trade, in the productions of the English school of painting, has experienced a vast augmentation; and it is even said that great quantities of these articles are sent to, and eagerly bought up, on the continent of Europe. See PAINTING. [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 752]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
