      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_64_66_89_Paper_Glass_Misc_Manufactures",
      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "any substance that serves to bind or unite by cohesion, as glue, solder, mortars, &c. In building, cement is a concretions of rubble mortars; the name is also applied to hydraulic mortars, impervious to water, such as Roman and Portland cements, puzzolano, &c. A composition for uniting metals is called solder, and the name cement is given to a lute or paste surrounding bodies in pots or crucibles for chemical purposes. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 90]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
