      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a confection; preserved or sweetened fruit. Scotch marmalade is presumed to be of oranges; and there are also marmalades of lemon, quince, and shaddock. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 253]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_sugars_sweeteners; processing_state=manufactured): Marmalade is a sugar preserve (cf. Succades, htc:0464). Layer-1 observations: 29 rows, 1811–1846. Series: KEW_CUST 4 ×29. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×29. Top routes: Canada → England ×14; Canada → Great Britain ×6; Canada → London ×5; Newfoundland → England ×2.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
