      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the dried berries of a West Indian tree, the *Eugenia Pimenta*, used as a spice in cookery, which have a flavour intermediate between pepper and cloves. The tree is exclusively cultivated in Jamaica, but of 36,061 cwts. imported thence in 1855, only 3,535 cwts. were entered for home consumption. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 300]",
