      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "charred or burnt wood, which is largely used for fuel on the Continent, and is also valued for making glass, steel, and as a deodorizer when powdered; cylinder charcoal obtained by distilling non-resinous woods is used in the manufacture of gunpowder. *See CARBON. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 95]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated fields — definition use: Auto-match had picked animal (bone) charcoal; the heading is wood charcoal (Canadian exports 1889–97).",
