        "@id": "htc:grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept"
      },
      "oe:observationCount/#resource": 13,
      "oe:groundingStatus/#resource": "local_concept_only",
      "oe:substanceHead/#resource": "Cubebs",
      "oe:processingState/#resource": "unspecified",
      "oe:ghostAcresDomain/#resource": "drugs_botanicals_chemicals",
      "oe:attestationBasis/#resource": "customs_enumerated",
      "oe:landBasis/#resource": "terrestrial_crop",
      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "cultivated",
      "oe:theodoridisBucket/#resource": "raw_materials",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_54_Medicinal_Pharmaceutical",
      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(Ger. kubeben; Fr. cubèbes; Ital. cubebi; Span. cubebas; Russ. kubebû; Arab. kebabeh; Javan. kumunkus; Hin. cubab-chinie). The produce of a plant, the *Piper cubeba* of Linnæus, and, under the Natural System, a species of *Piperaceæ*. It is cultivated in Java, and grows also in Penang and other parts of the East Indies. Specimens of cubebs from Ceylon were shown in the Exhibition of 1862. It is a small unripe fruit, dried like a pepper-corn, but somewhat longer. Cubebs have a hot, pungent, aromatic, slightly bitter taste, and a characteristic odour. They should be chosen large, fresh, sound, and the heaviest that can be procured. When cubebs have been kept long, especially in powder, they lose a portion of their volatile oil, on which, it appears, their medicinal properties depend. [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 555]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals): Named materia medica (castoreum, ginseng, cubebs, scammony, maidenhair, liquorice juice, quassia, cocculus indicus, serpentary, asafoetida, cantharides, hellebore, pipsissewa, ipecacuanha) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 13 rows, 1856–1866. Series: HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×13. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×13. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×3; Other Parts → United Kingdom ×3; Holland → United Kingdom ×2; France → United Kingdom ×1.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n555"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/15191"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n257"
        }
      ],
      "oe:firstAttested/#resource": 1856,
      "oe:lastAttested/#resource": 1866,
