      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_28_Metalliferous_Ores",
      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an important mineral. The green oxide furnishes a valuable colour for oil-painting, enamel, and porcelain. Chrome iron ore forms the basis of many of the coloured preparations of chrome used in dyeing, and for the production of chromate of potash. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 101]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_metallic_ores; processing_state=raw_ore): Ore/concentrate heading (chromite / chromate of iron in tons; metal 'contained in ore, matte, regulus'; pyrites); belongs with Metallic Ores & Concentrates like its sibling headings. Layer-1 observations: 13 rows, 1895–1901. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×10. Units: Tons ×13. Top routes: Canada → United States ×3; Canada → All Countries ×2; Ontario → All Countries ×2; Quebec → All Countries ×2.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
