      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a dye-stuff prepared from the red pulp of the seeds of the *Bixa orellana*, which enters into commerce under two forms, flag and roll. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 24]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_natural_dyestuffs): Named dye or pigment (annotto, orchella, weld, rock moss = orchil lichen per Mortimer 1823 s.v. ROCK MOSS 'See ORCHILLA', vermilion, zaffre, verdigris, lampblack) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 6 rows, 1800–1834. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×4; KEW_CUST 4 ×2. Units: CWTS (Hundredweights) ×4; Hundredweights.Quarters.Pounds ×2. Top routes: Canada → England ×2; World → United Kingdom ×1; Portugal and Madeira → United Kingdom ×1; Ireland → United Kingdom ×1.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
