      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_05_Vegetables_and_Fruit",
      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the *Tuber cibarium*, a fungus found in the earth beneath trees, especially oaks, beeches, and hawthorns. Being nutritious, fragrant, and stimulating in its properties, the truffle is a common ingredient in sauces and made dishes. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 402]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_fruits_nuts_vegetables): Named fruit, nut or vegetable left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 5 rows, 1800–1800. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×5. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×5. Top routes: France → United Kingdom ×1; Holland → United Kingdom ×1; World → United Kingdom ×1; Germany → United Kingdom ×1.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
