        "@value": "a kind of small dry hard water biscuit chiefly made in the United States; a firework. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 124]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_cereals_grains; processing_state=manufactured; wd_term=cracker; wd_relation=skos:closeMatch): Farinaceous preparations (macaroni, vermicelli, crackers/biscuit, starch, dextrine) belong with Cereals; other starch headings (htc:1561, htc:1572) are already here. Verified Wikidata anchor retained as closeMatch (the heading is the plural trade article). Layer-1 observations: 5 rows, 1811–1841. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×5. Units: Barrels ×4; Kegs ×1. Top routes: Quebec QC → Great Britain ×2; Montreal and Quebec → Great Britain ×1; Montreal and Quebec → British North America ×1; Montreal and Quebec → New South Wales ×1.",
