      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_54_Medicinal_Pharmaceutical",
      "oe:isAggregate/#resource": false,
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the commercial name for various blistering beetles, often termed Spanish flies; but which are also imported from China, Russia, Sicily, and Germany. The large genus *Mylabris* furnishes many insects possessing strong vesicatory powers. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 79]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:editorialNote": [
        {
          "@value": "Curated classification (group=grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals): Named materia medica (castoreum, ginseng, cubebs, scammony, maidenhair, liquorice juice, quassia, cocculus indicus, serpentary, asafoetida, cantharides, hellebore, pipsissewa, ipecacuanha) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 4 rows, 1800–1800. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×4. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×4. Top routes: Holland → United Kingdom ×1; Italy → United Kingdom ×1; World → United Kingdom ×1; Germany → United Kingdom ×1.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
