        "@value": "or wormwood, is the produce of *Artemisia absinthium*, which is much used in medicine for its bitter properties. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 14]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 14.",
