        {
          "@value": "Cusparia Bark",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an aromatic bitter bark, obtained in South America from the *Galipea cusparia*, or *officinalis*; a false Angostura bark, of dangerous properties, is peeled from the *Strychnos nux vomica* in India. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 24]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 24.",
