      "oe:landBasis/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "The *dhaura*, *dhauri*, *dhavada*, *hesel*, *bákli*, *arma*, *vellay naga*, *chiriman*, etc. A large deciduous pas Tree tree of the Sub-Himalayan tracts from the Ravi eastward to Central and Southern India. Ascends to 3,000 feet in altitude. Dhaura GUM is used in calico-printing and has been suggested as likely to be useful to dyers in England (*Journ. Chem. Soc. [Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 82]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs Unenumerated). Attested in: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 82.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/b31361584/page/n82"
        }
      ]
    },
