          "@value": "mosaic gold",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "stannic sulfide",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a metallic powder resembling gold-dust. The principal uses of bronze colours are for japanning and bronzing tin and iron goods, statues, castings, paper machine work, printing, ornamental painting, and such like purposes. *See LEAF METAL. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 64]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0010 (Other Articles). Attested in: 1866 British Customs Commodities List (Danika / HGIS Lab), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 64.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
