      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_29_Crude_Animal_Vegetable_Materials",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a ruby-coloured astringent gum-resin obtained in India from the Dhak-tree (*Butea frondosa*) which affords a powerful and permanent dye. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 69]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 69.",
