          "@value": "Chillies and Cayenne Pepper",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "*Guinea pepper*, is of three sorts, viz. 1. *Capsicum annuum*, the common long-podded capsicum. 2. *Capsicum baccacum*, the bird-pepper, grows nearly five feet high; the leaves are of a lucid green. This is the Cayenne-pepper. 3. *Capsicum grossum*, the bell-pepper. [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 200]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0408 (Spices Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 200.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
