      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "thin cakes baked on a griddle or the embers of a wood fire, made of the pulp or starchy matter of the roots of the cassava or manioc, which form a considerable article of food in tropical countries. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 86]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0408 (Spices Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 86.",
