      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_05_Vegetables_and_Fruit",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an esculent (*Apium graveolens*), the blanched footstalks of the leaves are eaten in England, and in many countries the leaves and seeds are used for soup. The seeds are also employed as a stimulant by the native medical practitioners of India. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 90]",
