      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "mineral_extraction",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_27_Crude_Fertilizers_and_Minerals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(_Craie_, Fr.; _Kreide_, Germ.) A friable carbonate of lime, white, opaque, soft, dull, or without any appearance of polish in its fracture. Its specific gravity varies from 2·4 to 2·6. It usually contains a little silica, alumina, and oxide of iron. It may be purified by trituration, and elutriation. [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
