          "@value": "Citronella Oil",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an essential oil obtained from the grass *Andropogon Citratum*, and chiefly imported from Ceylon. Another species, *A. schænanthus*, or *Cymbogon schænanthus*, furnishes the lemon-grass oil. *See LEMON GRASS. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 103]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0124 (Oil Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 103.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n103"
        }
