      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_27_Crude_Fertilizers_and_Minerals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(GER. *Englisches pflaster*. DU. *Engelsch pleister*. DA. *Engelskt plaster*. SW. *Engelskt pläster*. FR. *Taffetas d'Angleterre*. IT. *Taffeta d'Inghilterra*. SR. *Tafetan embalsamado de Inglaterra*. PORT. *Tafeta de Inglaterra*. LAT. *Emplastrum Anglicanum glutinans*,) a glutinous salve laid on fine black silk, and used as a healing plaster for slight sores. [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 255]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 255, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 123.",
