      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a valuable resin of two kinds, obtained in India, the white from the *Valeriana Indica* and *Shorea robusta*, and the black from *Canarium commune*: a name sometimes given in Scotland to a miner. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 132]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0220 (Gum Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 132.",
