          "@value": "Fennel Seed",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an umbelliferous plant, the *Anethum fœniculum dulce*, cultivated on the Continent as a pot-herb, and for the seeds and essential oil obtained from them. The seed is used in the manufacture of gin, and in medicine as a carminative. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 162]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
