      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_07_Coffee_Tea_Cocoa_Spices",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a plant, native of the South of France, the *Trigonella Fœnum Græcum*, the seeds of which are emollient; poultices made of the flour are employed in veterinary practice, and the Arabs use it in fomentations. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 162]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0408 (Spices Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 162, Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 411.",
