      "oe:landBasis/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a name, in the Eastern archipelago for the cotton down enveloping the seeds of the silk cotton-tree, *Bombax pentandrum*. It is used by the poor inhabitants for stuffing chairs, pillows, &c., but is seldom or never used for beds, it being thought unwholesome to sleep upon. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 224]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0822 (Esparto and other Vegetable Fibres for making Paper). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 224.",
