      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the floral leaves of the *Lavandula vera*, which are very fragrant. The compound spirit or tincture of lavender, is given in falutness or looseness of spirits, as a stimulant cordial. It is known as red lavender drops. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 235]",
