      },
      "oe:groundingStatus/#resource": "document_attested_grounded",
      "oe:ghostAcresDomain/#resource": "minerals_metals_energy",
      "oe:landBasis/#resource": "mineral",
      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "mineral_extraction",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_27_Crude_Fertilizers_and_Minerals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "(Eng. and Fr.; _Lazulith_, Germ.); is a blue vitreous mineral, crystallizing in rhomboidal dodecahedrons; spec. grav. 2·76 to 2·94; scratches glass; affords a little water by calcination; fusible into a white glass; dissolves in acids with loss of colour; solution leaves an alkaline residuum, after being treated with carbonate of ammonia, filtered, evaporated, and calcined. It consists of silica, 35·8; [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:1905 (Minerals Unenumerated). Attested in: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 236.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
        {
