      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_05_Vegetables_and_Fruit",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a tropical fruit, the produce of trees of the *Mangifera* family, of which there are many cultivated varieties, although only two distinct species of tree. The fruit of the finer kinds have a rich perfumed grateful flavour; while others are so stringy and unpleasant as not to be eatable. The fruit is pickled and preserved, and made into a cloutney. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 250]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0402 (Fruit Raw unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 250.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n250"
        }
      ],
      "skos:closeMatch": [
