      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_24_Cork_and_Wood",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "the yellowish wood of tho olive-tree which takes a good polish and, being beautifully feathered, is worked up into small ornamental fancy articles: in France and other parts of the Continent, it is used as a building wood. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 277]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
