      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "cultivated",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_53_Dyeing_Tanning_Colouring",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "and PRUSSIATE OF POTASH, are two important articles of chemical manufacture, which must be considered together. The first is called by English chemists, _Ferrocyanodide of iron_, the _Cyanure ferroso-ferrique_ of Berzelius; _Eisenblausaures eisenoxyd_, or _eisencyanür_ + _eisencyanid_, Germ.; [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs Unenumerated). Attested in: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562), Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 816.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
