      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "or **ROSALGAR**, (GER. *Rauschgelb*. DU. and DA. *Rusgeel*. SW. *Rauschgelb*. FR. *Réalgar*, *Réagal*. IT. *Risigallo*. SP. *Rejalgar*. PORT. *Rosalgar*. RUS. *Krasnoi arsenik*. POL. *Sandaraka*. LAT. *Risigallum*,) generally called *redorpiment*, is of two kinds, native and factitious. [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 845]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs Unenumerated). Attested in: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 845, P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 327.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
