      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "forest_harvest",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_24_Cork_and_Wood",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "an odoriferous wood, the produce of several species of *Santalum*, in India and the Pacific islands, of which there are two commercial kinds, the white, probably the outer layers of the wood, and the yellow, or citron, the inner wood. The odour is very strong, rose-like, and enduring. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 340]",
