      },
      "oe:groundingStatus/#resource": "document_attested_local",
      "oe:ghostAcresDomain/#resource": "drugs_botanicals_chemicals",
      "oe:landBasis/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "is a pigment prepared from a black juice secreted by certain glands of the cuttle-fish, which the animal ejects to darken the water when it is pursued. One part of it is capable of making 1000 parts of water nearly opaque. All the varieties of this mollusca secrete the same juice; [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs Unenumerated). Attested in: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 348.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "oe:dictionarySource/#resource": [
        {
          "@id": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n348"
        }
      ]
    },
