      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_27_Crude_Fertilizers_and_Minerals",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a soft, unctuous, magnesian mineral, used by the Chinese for making figures, and suitable for statuary and decorative purposes. *See SOAPSTONE. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 372]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:1905 (Minerals Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 372, Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562).",
