      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "SITC4_03_Fish_and_Seafood",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "a preparation of white poulrets, a famous Indian fish, which is much esteemed as a breakfast relish. The fish are cut in transverse slices, and preserved in kegs with the acid pulp of the tamarind fruit. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 383]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
