      },
      "oe:groundingStatus/#resource": "document_attested_grounded",
      "oe:ghostAcresDomain/#resource": "drugs_botanicals_chemicals",
      "oe:landBasis/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:harvestMode/#resource": "unclassified",
      "oe:sitcCode/#resource": "oe:sitcUnassigned",
      "skos:definition": {
        "@value": "is a rare metal, first discovered by Klaproth, in the black mineral called _pechblende_, found in a mine near Johann-Georgen-Stadt, in Saxony, and which is a sulphuret of uranium. A double phosphate of uranium and copper, called _green uranite_, and _uran mica_, occurs in Cornwall. [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0054 (Dye Stuffs Unenumerated). Attested in: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562), P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 516.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
